Opaque focus ramp width (dcsvr_two_layers_alpha=3, after 0031; native/quadviews/dcsvr_twolayer_ps.hlsl, dcsvr_live.h): the
user's flight of 2026-11-23 showed the flicker of the focus rectangle again in the right eye ("solid at the edges, fading
toward the centre"), the one 0024 (alpha 1, no blending) had removed. At edge blend 0.2 0031's ramp is the composition's
own band, so the focus layer stores the focus colour with the composition's fade as alpha: mode 0 (Standard) in all but
the corners, and whatever the runtime shows of its periphery layer under the focus on some frames shows again, weighted
by 1 - alpha. New key dcsvr_two_layers_opaque_ramp (live, settings.cfg): the ramp's width in the focus radius, taken as
set (no longer widened to the composition's band), default 0.4 (0031 unchanged at edge blend up to 0.2); 0: alpha 1 over
the whole rectangle and the layer submitted without blend flags (0024, live too). The width reaches the focus pass as
dcsvrEdge.w = 1 + width. Start-up log line "DCSVR two layers: opaque focus alpha ramp ...", reload line names the change.
